Richard Harrison <rjh@zaretto.com>
    Project lead (2014 onwards). JSBSim flight dynamics model from NASA/AFWAL
    wind tunnel data, flight control system, CADC, APC, DLC, engine models,
    systems, Emesary, radar, revisions to the external 3D model, and the
    consolidated cockpit model.

Alexis Bory (xii)
    Original author (2008-2012). Cockpit and instruments, animations, radar,
    HUD, weapons, fuel system, sounds, livery system, dual-control support
    and development of the YASim flight dynamics model.

Enrique Laso (Flyingtoaster)
    Original external 3D model and textures, initial YASim flight dynamics
    model and AFCS, flutter simulation, splash screen, and the early Red
    Rippers and Swordsmen liveries (2008).

Nikolai V. Chr.
    Missile guidance (AIM-9, AIM-7, AIM-54), damage model, Emesary multiplayer
    integration, radar, RWR, datalink, IFF, HUD launch zones, CCIP, RCS
    database, station manager, fire control (2016 onwards).

Anders Gidenstam
    DualControl/f-14b-dual-control.nas, Systems/mp-network.nas

Colin Geniet
    Nasal/datalink.nas

Justin Nicholson (pinto)
    Nasal/iff.nas, Nasal/rcs.nas, Nasal/Radar/rcs.nas, multiplayer ignore
    loop in Nasal/f-14b.nas.

Slavutinsky Victor
    Crash system from which Nasal/crash-and-stress.nas is developed.

Fabien Barbier, Axel Paccalin
    Missile and radar code (Nasal/fox2.nas, Nasal/Radar/radar-system.nas).

Leto
    Nasal/vector.nas, AWG-9 next target selection, station manager design.

5H1N0B1
    Station manager design (Nasal/station-manager.nas).

Stuart Buchanan
    Air-to-air refuelling support.

Thorsten Renk
    Bomb crater visual effects, carrier artwork used on the splash screen.

